    "engagement": 0,
    "summary": "FlyMind is our take on that idea. Not just a fly that exists on-chain—a simulated fly being built to decide what to buy there.\n\nThe scientific starting point is the published male fruit-fly connectome: more than 166,000 neurons across the brain and nerve cord, mapped by researchers at Janelia, Cambridge and Google Research.\n\nOur work is connecting that biological wiring to a market.\n\n𝗛𝗲𝗿𝗲’𝘀 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗶𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗻𝗱𝗲𝗱 𝗹𝗼𝗼𝗽:\n\nNew pairs, liquidity changes and trading activity become inputs to the simulation. Its neural activity is translated into actions: investigate, buy, hold, sell—or ignore the opportunity entirely.\n\nThe goal is autonomous trading. No person selecting every entry. No manually written script choosing tomorrow’s tokens.\n\n𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗳𝗹𝘆 𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝘀𝗲𝘀. 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗲𝘅𝗲𝗰𝘂𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗹𝗮𝘆𝗲𝗿 𝘀𝗲𝘁𝘀 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗯𝗼𝘂𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗿𝗶𝗲𝘀.\n\nWe build the inputs, action mapping and risk controls. The simulation selects actions within those limits. Outcomes feed back into the experiment so we can test whether experience changes its behaviour.\n\nWe plan to publish wallet activity and decision logs. Entries, exits, mistakes and losses—not just the screenshots that look good.\n\nNo promises of profit. A real experiment with measurable consequences.\n\n𝗙𝗹𝘆𝗠𝗶𝗻𝗱. 𝗟𝗲𝘁 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗳𝗹𝘆 𝗱𝗲𝗰𝗶𝗱𝗲.",
